.B class socketio.KafkaManager(url=\(aqkafka://localhost:9092\(aq, channel=\(aqsocketio\(aq, write_only=False, logger=None, json=None)
Kafka based client manager.
.sp
This class implements a Kafka backend for event sharing across multiple
processes.
.sp
To use a Kafka backend, initialize the \fBServer\fP \%<#\:socketio\:.Server> instance as
follows:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
url = \(aqkafka://hostname:port\(aq
server = socketio.Server(client_manager=socketio.KafkaManager(url))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBurl\fP \-\- The connection URL for the Kafka server. For a default Kafka
store running on the same host, use \fBkafka://\fP\&. For a highly
available deployment of Kafka, pass a list with all the
connection URLs available in your cluster.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchannel\fP \-\- The channel name (topic) on which the server sends and
receives notifications. Must be the same in all the
servers.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwrite_only\fP \-\- If set to \fBTrue\fP, only initialize to emit events. The
default of \fBFalse\fP initializes the class for emitting
and receiving. A write\-only instance can be used
independently of the server to emit to clients from an
external process.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogger\fP \-\- a custom logger to log it. If not given, the server logger
is used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBjson\fP \-\- An alternative JSON module to use for encoding and decoding
packets. Custom json modules must have \fBdumps\fP and \fBloads\fP
functions that are compatible with the standard library
versions. This setting is only used when \fBwrite_only\fP is set
to \fBTrue\fP\&. Otherwise the JSON module configured in the
server is used.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B close_room(room, namespace=None)
Remove all participants from a room.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
