.TP
.B class socketio.AsyncRedisManager(url=\(aqredis://localhost:6379/0\(aq, channel=\(aqsocketio\(aq, write_only=False, logger=None, json=None, redis_options=None)
Redis based client manager for asyncio servers.
.sp
This class implements a Redis backend for event sharing across multiple
processes.
.sp
To use a Redis backend, initialize the \fBAsyncServer\fP \%<#\:socketio\:.AsyncServer> instance as
follows:
.INDENT 7.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
url = \(aqredis://hostname:port/0\(aq
server = socketio.AsyncServer(
    client_manager=socketio.AsyncRedisManager(url))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B Parameters
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBurl\fP \-\- The connection URL for the Redis server. For a default Redis
store running on the same host, use \fBredis://\fP\&.  To use a
TLS connection, use \fBrediss://\fP\&. To use Redis Sentinel, use
\fBredis+sentinel://\fP with a comma\-separated list of hosts
and the service name after the db in the URL path. Example:
\fBredis+sentinel://user:pw@host1:1234,host2:2345/0/myredis\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchannel\fP \-\- The channel name on which the server sends and receives
notifications. Must be the same in all the servers.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwrite_only\fP \-\- If set to \fBTrue\fP, only initialize to emit events. The
default of \fBFalse\fP initializes the class for emitting
and receiving. A write\-only instance can be used
independently of the server to emit to clients from an
external process.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogger\fP \-\- a custom logger to log it. If not given, the server logger
is used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBjson\fP \-\- An alternative JSON module to use for encoding and decoding
packets. Custom json modules must have \fBdumps\fP and \fBloads\fP
functions that are compatible with the standard library
versions. This setting is only used when \fBwrite_only\fP is set
to \fBTrue\fP\&. Otherwise the JSON module configured in the
server is used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBredis_options\fP \-\- additional keyword arguments to be passed to
\fBRedis.from_url()\fP or \fBSentinel()\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 7.0
.TP
.B async close_room(room, namespace=None)
Remove all participants from a room.
.sp
Note: this method is a coroutine.
